Subject: [PATCH 16/16] Count tokens locally, with one bounded wait

Reason: On 2026-11-09 a desktop correction took 40 minutes around one 52-second
LLM call. The machine had no `tokcount` and could not reach Google, so every
uncached text waited out the connect timeouts of Gemini's `countTokens` before
falling back to the estimate, and nothing was logged. The Nonoka X desktop now
installs `tokcount` as a required tool, so the network fallback is gone: the
chain is the local binary, then the estimate, and any error falls through at
once. One count is capped at 10 seconds over everything that can block,
start-up and the pipe write included. A timeout gives up on the binary for the
rest of the process, with one warning, so a hang costs one wait. Shared with
the cloud without harm: it stops at `stable.json` and never counts tokens.

Removal: Delete once upstream stops counting tokens over the network and bounds
the local counter.

